      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KYCORDEN (9) is still a maiden but has the hoof on the till after four straight placings. Produced a strong performance last time when he came from this barrier to just miss out at this circuit and distance. If things go his way he could break through. LOUTHPARKSCHOONER (10) made it two consecutive wins last time out when he led and kept going to get home 4.7 metres at Penrith. Draws on the back row but if he gets the gaps he is going well enough to land the hat trick. HUNGRY JOE (7) has been coming from the back row of late and did manage a second three back at Penrith. Can measure up here. KEAYANG HARLOW (4) disappointed last time but went close from this barrier here two back so is worth another chance.",
